cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "k4m-bound: a Lean formalization of a log-polynomial bound for |K_{4m}(Z)| from the Alpöge archive's Selmer estimate"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Gross
    given-names: Ryland
repository-code: "https://github.com/rgrossharv/k4m-bound"
license: Apache-2.0
date-released: 2026-11-21
keywords:
  - Lean 4
  - formalization
  - algebraic K-theory
  - Selmer groups
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 derivation of log |K_{4m}(Z)| <= C (m+1)^A from the Selmer-length
  estimate UpperTheory.V.SmallClassNumbers.bound in the Lean archive
  accompanying Alpöge's announcement, together with a sorry-free proof that
  the archive's Selmer group ShaU equals the classical Selmer group (continuous
  H^1 with textbook local conditions, stated in local Galois cohomology). The
  K-theory comparison is an explicit hypothesis. Prepared with substantial AI
  assistance.
references:
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Salmons
        given-names: Aki
    title: "Uniform Selmer lengths and integral K-theory: an exact dictionary and conditional bounds"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/akisalmons/selmer-k-theory-note"
  - type: software
    authors:
      - family-names: Alpöge
        given-names: Levent
    title: "Lean development accompanying the announced proof of the Riemann Hypothesis"
    year: 2026
    url: "https://github.com/leanprover-community/riemann-hypothesis"
